>> title: Chili con Carne, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, chiles, texas, one-pot, stew, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: chili-con-carne
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: chili, bowl of red, Texas red, chili no beans, slow cooker chili, crockpot chili, crock pot chili con carne
>> servings: 6
>> time: 8 hr 40 min
>> slack: forgiving — the chile is bloomed in the skillet before the machine goes on, because there is no fixing a scorched one later
>> step.2: brown 12 min, in two batches
>> step.3: soften, then bloom the chile off the heat
>> step.4: simmer on low, 8 hr
>> step.5: thicken on high, lid off

Written for low, eight hours. This is the dish the machine is sold on in American home cooking, and ours is a bowl of red — no beans at all, which happens to remove the one real hazard of a slow-cooked chili: dried red kidney beans carry a toxin a low setting may never get hot enough to destroy, and would have to be boiled hard for ten minutes in fresh water first. There are none here. The stock comes down to a third, because nothing boils away.

Brown @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1/2-in dice), @kosher salt{2%tsp} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #skillet{} for ~brown{12%min}, in two batches with room around every piece.

Soften @yellow onion{1%large}(chopped), @garlic{6%cloves}(minced) in the same skillet, then pull it off the heat and stir in @ancho chile powder{1/4%cup}(30 g; pure ground chile, not a chili-powder blend), @ground cumin{1%Tbs}, @dried oregano{1%tsp} with @&(~1)browned beef{} — thirty seconds in the residual heat is the whole bloom, and chile scorched here is bitter for the rest of the day.

Slow cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{1%cup}(240 mL), @crushed tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g), @cider vinegar{1%Tbs} in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{8%hr}, lid on. A cup of stock against three looks wrong in the pot at hour one and is right at hour eight.

Thicken @&(~1)chili{} on high with the lid off, stirring in @masa harina{2%Tbs}(20 g; slaked in a little cold water) for ~thicken{20%min}, until a spoon dragged through leaves a track.
